    "event_description": "<p><br /></p>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><strong>Connect with the Wisdom of Winter</strong></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">As the days shorten and the air cools, join us for an evening designed to <strong>embrace winter&rsquo;s calm, grounding energy</strong>. This gentle introductory workshop invites you to slow down, soften your mind and reconnect with your body through <strong>Qigong, breathwork and quiet reflection.</strong></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Guided by nature coach<strong> Simon Lamb</strong>, you&rsquo;ll explore Qigong the <strong>ancient Chinese practice of cultivating vitality from within</strong>. Rooted in traditional Chinese medicine, Qigong teaches that when we create flow in the body, we create flow in life. Together, we&rsquo;ll tune into that sense of movement and ease, practicing beside the river as winter unfolds around us.</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><strong>No gym kit or experience needed.</strong> Simply come as you are, leave your shoes at the door and wrap yourself in the restorative energy of the season. We&rsquo;ll end with a warming moment of community and a cup of tea to send you back into the night feeling settled, centered and deeply connected.</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">What to wear:</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Comfortable, loose-fitting clothing and an extra layer to stay cosy at the end.</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">About Simon Lamb:</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Simon, Founder of WildKin, is a nature coach who helps people reconnect with themselves, each other and the natural world. His work blends movement, breathwork, mindfulness and coaching. It is grounded in training across qigong, nature connection and the Bio Leadership Project.</div>",
