    "event_title": "Sensory Tea Ceremony ",
    "event_description": "<p><br /></p>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Unwind as Lera, a devoted Student of the Leaf, guides you through a <strong>Chadao tea ceremony</strong> - a sacred practice used for centuries by Daoist sages and Buddhist monks for <strong>transformation and inner exploration.</strong></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">In this ceremony, tea becomes more than a drink it is a doorway. A doorway to slowing down, connecting deeply to presence and moving from the mind into the heart. Lera holds this sacred space with care, allowing you to savour, sense and simply be.</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Join us to <strong>experience the gentle power of tea</strong> as a plant medicine, nurturing vitality, inspiration and love. This is your invitation to pause, breathe and reconnect with the intimacy of life itself.</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Please note. During the Winter months, the Bishops Park gate to Fulham Pier will be closed from 6.30pm, and Bishop&rsquo;s Park itself will close at 7pm. Those joining us for events should use the Thames Path pathway from Stevenage Road to access Fulham Pier. Use what3words &lsquo;stars.boat.faster&rsquo; to guide you to the pathway.</div>",
    "event_summary": "A gentle tea-led journey from the mind into the heart.",
