    "event_title": "Mind to Motion Boxing Workshop ",
    "event_description": "<p data-start=\"89\" data-end=\"434\">Join us for a practical and uplifting wellbeing experience, designed to help you stress less and live longer. This energising workshop combines a guided wellbeing talk with a high-energy boxing session, giving you the tools to calm your mind, release tension and build everyday resilience.</p>\n<p data-start=\"89\" data-end=\"434\">Led by Gary Hanley, Founder of Mind to Motion CIC, Mental Health First Aider and Boxing Coach, this workshop offers a supportive, stigma-free space to boost your wellbeing and connect with others in the community.</p>\n<p data-start=\"436\" data-end=\"464\">Your session includes:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"465\" data-end=\"802\">\n<li data-start=\"465\" data-end=\"646\">\n<p data-start=\"467\" data-end=\"646\">Guided Wellbeing Talk &ndash; Stress Less, Live Longer<br data-start=\"521\" data-end=\"524\" /> Learn simple, proven techniques to manage stress, support your mental wellbeing and feel more grounded in daily life.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"647\" data-end=\"802\">\n<p data-start=\"649\" data-end=\"802\">High-Energy Boxing Fitness &ndash; No experience required<br data-start=\"706\" data-end=\"709\" /> Move, punch and strengthen your body in a fun and empowering session suitable for all levels.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1143\">Equipment: Please bring your own gloves if you have them - if not, we&rsquo;ll have gloves&nbsp;you can borrow.</p>\n<p>Price: &pound;10 per person<br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Why not extend your visit with something to eat or drink before, during, or after the workshop? Riverside Market offers casual bites, from&nbsp;salads to burgers, pizza to cocktails. For something more refined, book a table at Brasserie Constance, our seasonal modern British brasserie by Adam Byatt.</p>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Please note: During the winter months, the Bishops Park gate to Fulham Pier closes at 6.30pm, and Bishop&rsquo;s Park closes at 7pm. Guests attending evening events should access Fulham Pier via the Thames Path, approached from Stevenage Road. Use what3words &lsquo;stars.boat.faster&rsquo; to guide you to the pathway.</div>",
    "event_summary": "Join us for a practical and uplifting workshop designed to help you stress less and live longer. Enjoy a guided wellbeing talk and boxing session. ",
